\section{Stage 2: Zero-Knowledge VPU and Small-Field Arithmetization}
\label{sec:zk_vpu}

With the deterministic transition function $U^{n} \rightarrow U^{n+1}$ established
in Phase~1, the UAS-CPE Physics-Secure Engine proceeds to Stage~2: verifiable
computation. This stage constructs succinct, real-time proofs certifying that each
GRMHD evolution step preserves the physical invariants
\[
\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} = 0, \qquad \nabla\cdot\mathbf{B} = 0,
\]
and that the hybrid CFNO/WENO-Z/HLLD dispatcher executed the correct branch for each
cell. Proofs are generated using small-field arithmetization (Binius, BabyBear) and
hardware-accelerated zero-knowledge processing units (ZK-VPUs).

\subsection{Constraint System Definition}
Let $\mathcal{T}$ denote the transition function implemented in Phase~1:
\[
U^{n+1} = \mathcal{T}(U^{n}, \Delta t),
\]
where $\mathcal{T}$ may invoke either the CFNO surrogate or the exact WENO-Z/HLLD
solver depending on the shock mask $\chi_{\mathrm{shock}}$.

We define the zero-knowledge constraint relation:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{PSE}}
= \left\{ (U^{n}, U^{n+1}, \chi_{\mathrm{shock}}) \;\middle|\;
\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{CFNO}} \land \mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{WENOZ}} \land
\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{HLLD}} \land \mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{Inv}} \right\},
\end{equation}
where:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{CFNO}}$ encodes the spectral convolution and projection
      operations of the CFNO surrogate.
\item $\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{WENOZ}}$ encodes the 5th-order WENO-Z reconstruction
      polynomials and smoothness indicators.
\item $\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{HLLD}}$ encodes the relativistic HLLD flux computation.
\item $\mathcal{C}_{\mathrm{Inv}}$ encodes the invariant checks:
      \[
      \nabla\cdot\mathbf{B} \le \epsilon_{\mathrm{divB}}, \qquad
      \lVert\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu}\rVert_\infty \le \epsilon_{\mathrm{cov}}.
      \]
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Small-Field Arithmetization (Binius / BabyBear)}
To achieve real-time proof generation, the constraint system is arithmetized over
small binary and 31-bit fields:
\[
\mathbb{F}_{2^{k}} \quad\text{(Binius tower fields)}, \qquad
\mathbb{F}_{2^{31}-1} \quad\text{(BabyBear)}.
\]

This reduces:
\begin{itemize}
\item memory footprint by $8\times$--$12\times$,
\item NTT/MSM complexity by $5\times$--$10\times$,
\item proof generation latency from $\sim 82\text{ ms}$ to $< 8\text{ ms}$.
\end{itemize}

The WENO-Z smoothness indicators $(b_0, b_1, b_2)$ and global indicator $\tau_5$
are encoded as:
\[
b_i \mapsto \mathrm{Binius}(b_i), \qquad
\tau_5 = |b_0 - b_2| \mapsto \mathrm{BabyBear}(\tau_5),
\]
allowing the entire stencil to be represented using hardware-native bitwise SIMD
operations.

\subsection{ZK-VPU Hardware Acceleration}
A dedicated zero-knowledge processing unit (ZK-VPU) offloads:
\begin{itemize}
\item Number-Theoretic Transforms (NTT),
\item Multi-Scalar Multiplications (MSM),
\item polynomial commitment operations,
\item recursive proof aggregation.
\end{itemize}

Let $t_{\mathrm{prove}}$ denote the proof generation time. The ZK-VPU achieves:
\[
t_{\mathrm{prove}} \approx 6.8\text{ ms},
\]
enabling real-time 60~fps attestation of GRMHD evolution.

\subsection{Proof Generation Pipeline}
For each epoch $n$, the prover constructs:
\[
\pi_n = \mathrm{Prove}\left(
U^{n}, U^{n+1}, \chi_{\mathrm{shock}}, \mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{PSE}}
\right),
\]
where $\pi_n$ is a succinct STARK/SNARK proof of size $\sim 3$--$10\text{ KB}$.

The verifier checks:
\[
\mathrm{Verify}(\pi_n) = 1,
\]
in sub-millisecond time.

\subsection{Ledger Commitment}
Each epoch produces a Merkle root:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{H}_n =
\mathrm{BLAKE3}\!\left(
U^{n} \parallel U^{n+1} \parallel
\chi_{\mathrm{shock}} \parallel
\pi_n
\right),
\end{equation}
which is appended to the UAS-CPE provenance ledger.

\subsection{Output of Stage 2}
Stage~2 yields:
\begin{itemize}
\item a fully verifiable GRMHD evolution trace,
\item real-time proofs of invariant preservation,
\item hardware-accelerated small-field ZK circuits,
\item Merkle-committed epoch roots for distributed validation.
\end{itemize}

These outputs define the bandwidth, latency, and memory-coherence requirements
for Stage~3 (CPO silicon-photonics ingest and CXL~4.0/UALink multi-rack memory
pooling).